{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1547327-heroes-and-other-supernaturals","id":1547327,"title":"Heroes and other Supernaturals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-30T03:16:32-08:00","id":1547327,"title":"Heroes and other Supernaturals","content":"How do heroes work when they encounter other supernatural creatures? For example, an Anathema of garlic that a hero place on a vampire,with what rating should we regard that? and how do the other gifts work, like Champion's Endurance? do they work or are the heroes just normal humans with no abilities whatsoever?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28580-madoglio14","name":"Madoglio14","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-30T04:26:02-08:00","id":1547328,"title":"","content":"Generally, heroes are just normal humans against other supernaturals (though they are a bit tougher thanks to their default Hard to Kill ability), though their ability to attract followers gives them another edge against supernaturals regardless of their nature. The Kinslayer Gift allows a Hero to use many of their powers (though not placing Anathema) on any creatures that have the Family Ties Condition to a Beast, but it only works on such individuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-19T08:14:23-08:00","id":1547830,"title":"","content":"Besides, from my understanding, Heroes usually tend to be completely disinterested in supernaturals that aren\u2019t either Beasts, or direct kin thereof. There are exceptions, naturally, but that\u2019s the general rule for the sorts of Heroes that Beasts tend to encounter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-19T15:16:08-08:00","id":1547837,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say disinterested as much as it gets to individual motivations. Heroes are characters that have their own internal narratives about what they do and why. It's all about how a given supernatural fits into that narrative; which can range from &quot;doesn't&quot; so the Hero ignores them completely, to, &quot;is just a well disguised Beast,&quot; to be killed off as well. A Hero that sees themselves as a righteous defender of their community from dangerous evil forces can't just let some vampires slide in and do whatever they want. That goes against the Hero's personal narrative. A Hero that's out to hunt and kill the biggest and baddest monsters might not give a moment's thought to some low level vampires just finding an easy meal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-24T22:26:14-08:00","id":1547943,"title":"","content":"And of course how the other Beast is interacting with other supernaturals. A handful of vampire might not interest a Kraven the Hunter while there's the bigger and fiercer Beast around, but if they're known to hangout or work together then the kindred might be put on the list either as potential obstacles, bait, or just part of the challenge for killing the Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-02T20:29:45-08:00","id":1548129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1547327-heroes-and-other-supernaturals?p=1547837#post1547837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say disinterested as much as it gets to individual motivations. Heroes are characters that have their own internal narratives about what they do and why. It's all about how a given supernatural fits into that narrative; which can range from &quot;doesn't&quot; so the Hero ignores them completely, to, &quot;is just a well disguised Beast,&quot; to be killed off as well. A Hero that sees themselves as a righteous defender of their community from dangerous evil forces can't just let some vampires slide in and do whatever they want. That goes against the Hero's personal narrative. A Hero that's out to hunt and kill the biggest and baddest monsters might not give a moment's thought to some low level vampires just finding an easy meal.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1547327-heroes-and-other-supernaturals?p=1547943#post1547943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And of course how the other Beast is interacting with other supernaturals. A handful of vampire might not interest a Kraven the Hunter while there's the bigger and fiercer Beast around, but if they're known to hangout or work together then the kindred might be put on the list either as potential obstacles, bait, or just part of the challenge for killing the Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s why I said \u2018usually\u2019, and specified in \u2018the sorts of Heroes that Beasts tend to encounter.\u2019 The sheer variety that could occur in Heroes, even with common trends being factored in, means that even <i>if</i> a non-Begotten Supernatural were to be opposed by one, they\u2019re not always going to go straight for the whole \u2018\u2019find\u2019/apply anathema, then attack\u2019 variety of routes that most of such Heroes prefer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-02T23:40:27-08:00","id":1548132,"title":"","content":"The problem is that the qualifiers don't really account for my response. There isn't really a &quot;usual&quot; here, even for Heroes that are focused on killing Beasts as antagonists for the game with the potential for Heroes without such focus existing in the broader world of the setting.<br /> <br /> They also can't place Anathema on non-Begotten anyway, so that isn't even part of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-04T13:38:07-08:00","id":1548201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1547327-heroes-and-other-supernaturals?p=1548129#post1548129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s why I said \u2018usually\u2019, and specified in \u2018the sorts of Heroes that Beasts tend to encounter.\u2019 The sheer variety that could occur in Heroes, even with common trends being factored in, means that even <i>if</i> a non-Begotten Supernatural were to be opposed by one, they\u2019re not always going to go straight for the whole \u2018\u2019find\u2019/apply anathema, then attack\u2019 variety of routes that most of such Heroes prefer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, the edge case isn't going to be a Hero seeing a Beast hanging out with a bunch of vampires and go, &quot;Eh sod the leeches I want the Garuda.&quot; Its gonna be a thing they factor into their approach, assuming they're not just &quot;I have the sword of destiny and all wickedness shall fall before my might! CHARGE!&quot; If the Beast has allies and the Hero finds out the Hero will factor it or else they're a very quick corpse. Afterall, not that they know it, but Heroes can't use Banes and Anathema on non-Beghotten most of the time. (I think there's a power or two that do mention working on other supernatural entities and you can probably apply stuff like the power that makes people into your followers on other supernaturals, but those are edge cases.) <br /> <br /> Is a Hero going to go out of their way to hunt supernaturals that aren't Beghotten or tied to them? That's gonna vary a lot based on the Hero's personal narrative, often the answer is no, but many might not even notice because its not like the abilities a Hero has that detect Beasts will alert them to the fact that their bartender at the pub they frequent is a Nephandi. And unless something has changed most Anathema aren't in the grouping that a Hero thinks they're applying. So one getting attacked by a werewolf isn't going to be, &quot;Okay I need to apply an anathema and then kill it,&quot; or &quot;I need to find a way to apply a power to it,&quot; it would be the much simpler, &quot;Am I being attacked by a werewolf? Do I have silver on me?&quot; Or for the other fun, &quot;What kills werewolves?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T01:59:38-07:00","id":1560881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madoglio14</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1547327-heroes-and-other-supernaturals#post1547327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do heroes work when they encounter other supernatural creatures? For example, an Anathema of garlic that a hero place on a vampire,with what rating should we regard that? and how do the other gifts work, like Champion's Endurance? do they work or are the heroes just normal humans with no abilities whatsoever?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple answer is, they get the shit kicked out of them.<br /> <br /> I don't remember if it's in the core book, or the player's guide, but this exact scenario plays out in the story chapter.<br /> <br /> The Hero is hunting a sea monster, and fashions a weapon out of a ship's anchor, believing that the Beast is vulnerable to it. Which, of course, it is, because of Anathema.<br /> <br /> What the Hero did not know, however, is the Beast was friends with a vampire, who shows up to rescue him. When the Hero tries to use his anchor against her, she promptly kills him with no effort.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------<br /> <br /> As far as I was able to figure out, a Hero's powers only increase when they deliver the killing blow to a Beast, and they only function when confronting a Beast.<br /> <br /> When pitted up against any other kind of monster, they seem to just be normal people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T03:12:33-07:00","id":1560882,"title":"","content":"As I noted in my first post on the thread (and that was over 1.5 years ago... it's OK to let old threads be), there's a few things that Heroes have over normal humans:<br /> <br /> 1) The Hard to Kill trait applies even if they're up against other supernaturals. It's not a huge deal, but it's something.<br /> <br /> 2) If they're aware of other supernatural threats, they aren't going to shirk away like normal humans and can stand up and apply all their skills at hunting Beasts to hunting anything else.<br /> <br /> 3) They can gain the ability to amass followers. Those followers aren't particularly special, but numbers means a lot and can cause number supernaturals their own issues.<br /> <br /> 4) There is a Hero power that lets them apply more of their powers to other supernaturals, but it's restricted to those that have the Family Ties Condition towards a Beast (which are going to be almost any supernatural that's close friends with one; the benefits to the Begotten and their allies are too big and they don't inherently know Heroes can abuse that bond). <br /> <br /> As the thread covered, it gets very individualized very quickly. Some Heroes are going to die easily if they go up against anything else because they're not prepared, and some can even the playing field significantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T20:08:14-07:00","id":1560919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1547327-heroes-and-other-supernaturals?p=1560882#post1560882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) If they're aware of other supernatural threats, they aren't going to shirk away like normal humans and can stand up and apply all their skills at hunting Beasts to hunting anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of their more glaring weaknesses, however, is that Heroes can't really sense the presence of other supernaturals, like they can with Beasts. They aren't connected to the Primordial Dream in the same way the Begotten are.<br /> <br /> That means other splats have the advantage of surprise, as they can reliable conceal themselves before going in for the attack.<br /> <br /> Also, Heroes are likely to write other splats off as being lesser threats than the Beast for a similar reason. The Beast is powerful enough to give off a distinct aura of malice that the Hero can feel in their dreams, so clearly they must be the main antagonist, while everyone else are just minions working under them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T20:48:02-07:00","id":1560922,"title":"","content":"I don't think anyone was trying to make the case the Heroes are some sort of truly epic badasses that can unload on anything they can apply their powers to with ease. At best they're on par with Tier 1 and 2 Hunters largely depending on how big of a following they can manage. Even a fairly experienced Hero isn't really that much of a threat to a PC Beast (esp. not a Brood of them). It's just that they are a threat at all because they are aware of the supernatural world around them and thus can apply human lateral thinking and problem solving skills fully along with the potential of having some additional edges normal humans don't get through their connection to the Primordial Dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T15:29:12-07:00","id":1560950,"title":"","content":"Also always good to remember you have other problems, other goals, and most Heroes are masters of causing collateral damage.<br /> <br /> If any hunter can cause a lot of harm to your life without being a physical threat, one that can harass you as consistently as a Hero is a particular problem.<br /> <br /> Victory will be easy, but not all that enjoyable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}